Your code has an error:  
❌ `a.length()` → `length` is a property, not a function, so it should be `a.length` (without parentheses).

### **Fixed Code:**
```js
let a = ["shlok", "krrish", "adavit"];
let b = prompt("Enter the name");

for (let c = 0; c < a.length; c++) {  // ✅ Use a.length instead of a.length()
  if (a[c] === b) {
    alert("You are in the list");
  }
}
```

### **Improved Version (with case insensitivity & better structure)**
```js
let a = ["shlok", "krrish", "adavit"];
let b = prompt("Enter the name").toLowerCase(); // Convert input to lowercase

if (a.some(name => name.toLowerCase() === b)) { // Check if name exists in array
  alert("You are in the list");
} else {
  alert("You are NOT in the list");
}
```

This version:
✅ Ignores case differences (`Shlok` and `shlok` will be treated the same).  
✅ Uses `.some()` for cleaner, more efficient checking.  

